dialogue trust_knight_3
title: The water carrier
trigger: Trust knight level=3
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  A peddler's cart passed the camp at dusk, heading for the holds. Since then the Knight has stood at the edge of the firelight with a folded scrap of bark paper, reading it over and over.
  * Bad news from the road? -> news
    do: AddTrust $with 4
  * Whatever it says, it won't read any different the tenth time. -> tenth
    do: AddTrust $with -2
  * You've been standing guard over a letter for an hour. Come and sit. -> guard
    do: AddTrust $with 5

node news hero
  News from home. The peddler carried it two holds over before anyone found a cart going our way. It's from my sister.
  -> letter

node tenth hero
  No. It reads the same every time. I keep hoping one of the words will change. It's from my sister.
  -> letter

node guard hero
  Guarding it. Ha. I suppose I am. Old habit. It's from my sister.
  -> letter

node letter hero
  She carries water for the hold. Up from the well, every morning, since we were small. She was carrying it the day I left for the arches. She waved with the bucket.
  -> levy

node levy hero
  The Captain's calling a levy. Everyone old enough to hold a spear, marched out to hunt the runaways who stole the Choir's caravan. That's us, Commander. That's this wagon.
  -> spear

node spear hero
  She's old enough now. If they put a spear in her hands and point her at this camp, I don't know what I do. I've thought about it all night and I still don't know.
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Knight folds the letter once more and holds it out, as though the Commander should be the one to keep it.
  * When the road reaches the holds, we go to her first. Before anything else. -> promised
    do: AddTrust $with 10
    do: SetFlag knight:sister_promised
  * Send word back with the next cart. Tell her to get out before the levy reaches her. -> warned
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag knight:sister_warned
  * We can't turn this wagon round for one hold. Not with the Captain behind us. -> denied
    do: AddTrust $with -4
    do: SetFlag knight:sister_denied

node promised hero
  First. You'd do that. For a water carrier you've never met. Then I'll hold you to it, Commander, the way the hold holds me to the oath.
  -> after

node warned hero
  Get out. She won't, she's too stubborn. But she'll read it, and she'll know I'm still standing, and that's something. I'll find a cart at first light.
  -> after

node denied hero
  One hold. That's my whole world you're counting there. But you're not wrong about the Captain. I'll stand where you need me. I'll just be looking back over my shoulder while I do.
  -> after

node after commander
  The Knight tucks the letter inside the shield's strap, flat against the iron, next to the words on the rim.
  -> close

node close hero
  Stand before the hold. I used to think that meant the gate. Maybe it means wherever she is.
